            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Another Peek Beyond the Point"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.088,
            0.265,
            0.109
          ],
          "content": "**Examples:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.113,
            0.844,
            0.215
          ],
          "content": "| 24 ÷ 100 = 0.24 | 678 ÷ 1000 = 0.678 |\n| --- | --- |\n| 12÷1000 = 0.012 | 12345÷1000 = 12.345 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_2_table_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.246,
            0.518,
            0.271
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "4.2 Decimal Multiplication"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.279,
            0.849,
            0.339
          ],
          "content": "？ **Example 1:** Arshad goes to a stationery shop and purchases 5 pens. If one pen costs ₹9.5 (9 rupees and 50 paisa), how much should he pay the shopkeeper?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.353,
            0.495,
            0.376
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "What operation must we use here?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.379,
            0.827,
            0.424
          ],
          "content": "We have to multiply 9.5 by 5, which is the same as adding 9.5, 5 times. That is $9.5 \\times 5 = 9.5 + 9.5 + 9.5 + 9.5 + 9.5 = 47.5.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.428,
            0.846,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": "We can also directly multiply the numbers by converting them into fractions."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.468,
            0.463,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": "9.5 is $\\frac { 9 5 } { 1 0 }$ and 5 is $\\frac { 5 } { 1 }$ as a fraction."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.508,
            0.418,
            0.545
          ],
          "content": "The cost of 5 pens $= { \\frac { 5 } { 1 } }   \\times   { \\frac { 9 5 } { 1 0 } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.548,
            0.846,
            0.587
          ],
          "content": "Recall that, to find the product of two fractions, we multiply the numerators and multiply the denominators."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.421,
            0.586,
            0.572,
            0.687
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{5}{1} \\times \\frac{95}{10} = \\frac{5 \\times 95}{1 \\times 10} = \\frac{475}{10} = 47.5",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.692,
            0.41,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": "The cost of 5 pens is ₹47.5."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.721,
            0.846,
            0.787
          ],
          "content": "**Example 2:** A car travels 12.5 km per litre of petrol. What is the distance covered with 7.5 litres of petrol? We have to multiply 12.5 by 7.5."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.791,
            0.498,
            0.81
          ],
          "content": "The distance covered = 12.5 × 7.5"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.334,
            0.816,
            0.665,
            0.854
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{125}{10} \\times \\frac{75}{10} = \\frac{125 \\times 75}{10 \\times 10} = \\frac{9375}{100} = 93.75",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.86,
            0.481,
            0.879
          ],
          "content": "The distance covered is 93.75 km."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.813,
